			<CaseStructure Bounds="615 180 235 235" DataType="Int32" Default="97" Id="96" Selected="98" UserSelectorBounds="68 0 100 17">
				<CaseStructure.Case Bounds="5 5 225 225" Id="97" Pattern="Default" />
				<CaseStructure.Case Bounds="5 5 225 225" Id="98" Pattern="2, 4">
					<Comment Bounds="10 10 205 122" Id="101" xmlns="http://www.ni.com/MocCommon">
						<p.Text>"If the DisplayExecution event\nwas generated because the\nexecution hit a breakpoint (2) or\nbecause the execution is breaking\non a run-time error (4), bring the\noperator interface application to\nthe front by setting the\nFront Panel.Open property of the\ntop-level VI to True."</p.Text>
					</Comment>
				</CaseStructure.Case>
				<CaseStructure.Selector Bounds="-4 60 13 10" Docking="Left" Id="99" Terminals="96=104, 97, 98" />
				<CaseStructure.Tunnel Bounds="-4 130 13 10" Docking="Left" Id="100" Terminals="96=106, 97, 98" />
			</CaseStructure>
			<Wire Id="104" Joints="N(91:c1t0v)|(207,245) N(99:96)|(611,245)" xmlns="http://www.ni.com/PlatformFramework" />
			<Comment Bounds="260 65 330 95" Id="105" xmlns="http://www.ni.com/MocCommon">
				<p.Text>"The Application Manager generates the DisplayExecution\nevent when TestStand starts a new execution that is not\ninitially hidden. It also generates the event when the\nexecution breaks.\n\nNote: This VI is marked to be reentrant since it is an\nActiveX event callback VI."</p.Text>
			</Comment>
			<Wire Id="106" Joints="N(92:c0t0v)|(379,315) N(100:96)|(611,315)" xmlns="http://www.ni.com/PlatformFramework" />
			<Wire Id="109" Joints="N(35:Value)|(40,205) h(90) v(15) N(91:instance in)|(135,220)" xmlns="http://www.ni.com/PlatformFramework" />
		</BlockDiagram>
